{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Four optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, and analytics (Mixpanel or any backend).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The dispatch cycle:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop.","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"Swidux","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Swidux"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"title":"Tutorials"},{"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/d